WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.062
Next question: how steep is the line?

00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:04.284
That's the slope.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.838
Pick two points on the line.

00:00:06.838 --> 00:00:11.989
For the stage, let's use the point zero, six, and the point four, three.

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:13.786
First, the run.

00:00:13.786 --> 00:00:15.948
We move four to the right.

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:17.611
That's four seconds.

00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:19.119
Then the rise.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:22.538
We move three down, so the rise is negative three.

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:28.346
Slope is rise over run: negative three over four, or negative three-fourths.

00:00:28.896 --> 00:00:29.829
That's the rate.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:34.320
Every second, the performer gets three-fourths of a meter closer to the mark.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.778
When a line goes up from left to right, the slope is positive.

00:00:38.778 --> 00:00:42.749
That's the pool, where the swimmer moves farther from the wall.

00:00:43.299 --> 00:00:46.128
When it goes down, the slope is negative.

00:00:46.128 --> 00:00:48.750
And when it's flat, the slope is zero.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.279
So rise over run tells you how fast the y-value changes, and which way it goes.
